implementationPlan.description:
A new scripts/local-runner/admission.mjs: inputs, re-validation and base consistency, plus rows A1-A2 in scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs.

Add the module's static import at the top of the test file, as every other local-runner module is imported (gotcha-local-runner-tests).

Header comment. CQ-R12 host admission turns one candidate into ONE Git tree object in the host repository. The candidate is validateImport's frozen manifest, from R09's importCandidate, applied to the protected base tree (R09b's exportSourceSnapshot().tree).
- Plumbing only. No ref is written and no working-tree or .git/index byte changes. Target branch writes stay in the wrappers' landing, so candidate Moe source cannot replace the active host controller.
- Hooks, fsmonitor, filters and helpers are disabled, and Git config and env are sanitized.
- Nothing from the repository (tests, package scripts, hooks, its own git binary) is ever executed.
- executionReady stays false and verified-local stays unavailable.

admitCandidate({repoDir, baseTree, candidate, git, timeoutMs = 120_000}):
- Input checks. Each failure throws ADMISSION_INPUT_INVALID (fixed-text MESSAGES and admissionError, in the module's idiom):
  - repoDir: an absolute path with no control character;
  - git: an ABSOLUTE path. A bare 'git' with cwd set to the repository lets Windows CreateProcess run a repository git.exe, the same issue as bug task-d72fe292;
  - baseTree: 40 or 64 hex;
  - timeoutMs: 1 to 600_000;
  - candidate: a frozen record whose key set is exactly {entries, digest}.
- Re-validate: validateImport(candidate.entries mapped back to {kind, path, executable, data} or {kind, path}) must give the same digest and, entry by entry, the same sha256. Otherwise throw ADMISSION_INPUT_INVALID; SNAPSHOT_* codes pass through.
- run = gitRunner(git, root, timeoutMs, {prefix: ['-c', `core.hooksPath=${emptyHooksDir}`, '-c', 'core.splitIndex=false'], env: {GIT_INDEX_FILE: tempIndex}, fail}).
  - The private temp dir comes from fs.mkdtemp(os.tmpdir() + '/moe-admission-'). It holds an empty hooks/ dir and the index, and is removed in a finally on every path.
  - Open the repository through openRepository, where refusal gives ADMISSION_REPOSITORY_UNSUPPORTED.
  - `rev-parse --show-object-format` must be sha1 or sha256, matching baseTree's length.
  - `rev-parse --verify --quiet --end-of-options <baseTree>^{tree}` must equal baseTree, else ADMISSION_BASE_INVALID.
- Base consistency, from `ls-tree -r -z --full-tree <baseTree>` parsed with LS_TREE-style records into path -> mode. Any violation gives ADMISSION_ENTRY_CONFLICT:
  - a delete must name a base blob of mode 100644 or 100755 (the R09 QA note: deletes are checked against the base);
  - a file may replace only such a blob, or add a new path;
  - with remaining = base minus deletes, no proper '/'-prefix of a file path may be a remaining path (nothing beneath a base file, symlink or gitlink);
  - a file path must not be a directory prefix of a remaining path.
  update-index --index-info would otherwise replace across D/F conflicts silently.
- Error handling: one fixed code per refusal, never a partial result; no path, byte or Git output in a message.

Rows (A prefix; skip only where noted):
- A1: each input refusal, including a bare 'git', a relative repoDir, an unfrozen candidate, an extra key, a tampered sha256 or digest, a data buffer edited after validateImport, and timeoutMs 0 or 600_001. No git is spawned: a logging git wrapper logs nothing; on win32 assert that the temp dir is gone.
- A2, a scratch repo built with the test's own git:
  - a base containing a, d/x, l (a symlink, POSIX only) and m (a gitlink, via update-index --cacheinfo 160000);
  - refusals for: deleting 'nope', 'd' or 'l'; a file at 'l' or 'm'; 'a/b' while a remains; a file 'd' while d/x remains;
  - deleting a with file 'a/b' is allowed;
  - an object-format mismatch, and baseTree being a blob or commit id, give ADMISSION_BASE_INVALID;
  - a repo with filter.x.clean in config.worktree (via extensions.worktreeConfig) gives ADMISSION_REPOSITORY_UNSUPPORTED.

The candidate tree in admission.mjs, plus rows A3-A4 (DoD 2).

1. Blobs:
   - write each file's data into the temp dir (blob-<n>, mode 0600);
   - run ONE `hash-object -w --no-filters --stdin-paths` with those temp paths on stdin. --no-filters: no clean filter, autocrlf or eol conversion; the path is a temp file, never a worktree path;
   - each printed id must equal a Node-computed object id: createHash(sha1 or sha256) of `blob <size>\0` + data, else ADMISSION_GIT_FAILED.
2. `read-tree <baseTree>` into the temp index (no -u or -m, so no worktree access).
3. `update-index -z --force-remove --stdin` with the delete paths, then `update-index -z --index-info` with `<100644|100755> <id>\t<path>\0` records.
4. `write-tree`; its id must be a full 40- or 64-hex id.
5. Resolve Object.freeze({baseTree, tree, digest: candidate.digest}).

The module never runs update-ref, commit, commit-tree, checkout, reset, merge, fetch, push, gc or hook. The step-4 envelope row pins the allowed set.

Error handling: any Git failure or a mismatch gives ADMISSION_GIT_FAILED with fixed text. The temp dir is removed on every path, including a throw from writing a blob file.

Rows:
- A3:
  - `git ls-tree -r <tree>` equals base minus deletes plus files, with the exec bit as mode 100755;
  - each blob's `cat-file blob` bytes equal the candidate data, including bytes that a .gitattributes `text eol=crlf` or a `filter=x` would have changed;
  - an empty candidate gives tree === baseTree;
  - two concurrent admissions of different candidates both succeed with their own trees.
- A4 (DoD 2): the worktree holds 'active controller' files: scripts/moe-agent.sh and scripts/local-runner/admission.mjs, as copies. The candidate modifies both and adds a file. After admission:
  - the worktree file bytes, the .git/index bytes, `for-each-ref` output, HEAD, and packed-refs (if any) are unchanged;
  - the real module file under test is unchanged (sha256 before and after);
  - no candidate file was executed: a candidate script that would write a marker if run leaves no marker;
  - the tree contains the candidate bytes;
  - admission.mjs imports only node: built-ins and ./ siblings, and has no dynamic import(); check it by a regex over its source.

Hostile-environment rows A5-A6 (DoD 1, DoD 3).

- A5, a hostile repository and host, using one scratch repo:
  - executable hooks writing a marker: post-index-change, reference-transaction, pre-commit, post-commit, post-checkout and fsmonitor-watchman, in .git/hooks AND in a dir named by a local core.hooksPath;
  - a local core.fsmonitor naming a marker script;
  - a package.json whose test, prepare and postinstall scripts write markers;
  - inherited GIT_DIR, GIT_INDEX_FILE (pointing at the real index), GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY, GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS ('core.hooksPath'='<marker dir>') and GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY/VALUE in process.env;
  - a HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME whose .gitconfig sets core.hooksPath, core.fsmonitor and a filter.
  Set the env inside the test and restore it in t.after. Admission succeeds into the right repository; no marker exists; and the real index, refs and worktree are unchanged.
  A local filter.x.clean marker gives ADMISSION_REPOSITORY_UNSUPPORTED, with no marker.
- A6, the envelope (POSIX only; skip on win32 with a reason). Pass as git a /bin/sh wrapper that appends argv and every GIT_* variable to a log, then execs the real git (the R09b hostile-wrapper technique). Every invocation must:
  - carry --no-replace-objects, -c protocol.allow=never, -c core.fsmonitor=false, -c core.hooksPath=<an empty dir inside the temp dir> and -c core.splitIndex=false;
  - have GIT_* exactly {GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL, GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT, GIT_INDEX_FILE inside the temp dir};
  - use only the subcommands rev-parse, config, ls-tree, hash-object, read-tree, update-index and write-tree.
  The temp dir no longer exists afterwards.

Error handling in the rows: a marker check reads the absence of files and never swallows an admission error.

implementationPlan.note:
A5 (DoD 1 and DoD 3) sets up a hostile repository and host:
- marker hooks (post-index-change, reference-transaction, pre/post-commit, post-checkout, fsmonitor-watchman) in .git/hooks AND in a local core.hooksPath dir;
- a local core.fsmonitor, and package.json test/prepare/postinstall scripts;
- inherited GIT_DIR/GIT_WORK_TREE/GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY aimed at a decoy repo, GIT_INDEX_FILE aimed at the real index, GIT_CONFIG_PARAMETERS (hooksPath), GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY/VALUE (fsmonitor) and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL/SYSTEM;
- a HOME and XDG_CONFIG_HOME config with hooksPath, fsmonitor and filter.x.clean.

A POSIX positive control first shows the fsmonitor and hooksPath hooks really fire outside the envelope. Admission then succeeds into the right repo (the decoy lacks the tree): no marker, and the worktree, .git minus objects/ and refs are unchanged. A local filter.x.clean gives ADMISSION_REPOSITORY_UNSUPPORTED with no marker. The marker dir has no space, because Git runs core.fsmonitor through the shell.

A6 (POSIX; skipped on win32 with a reason) pins, through a /bin/sh logging wrapper:
- the FULL prefix on every call: R09b's GIT_PREFIX, safe.directory, then core.hooksPath=<temp>/hooks, core.splitIndex=false and index.sparse=false;
- the exact GIT_* set, with GIT_INDEX_FILE=<temp>/index;
- the subcommand set {rev-parse, config, ls-tree, hash-object, read-tree, update-index, write-tree};
- that the temp dir is gone.

Also trimmed admission.mjs by 2 lines (readInput now returns inside its try, as source-export does; the hooks dir is inlined). No behavior change; A1-A6 pass. Size so far: source-export +18/-10, admission 153, tests +219, so 400 changed lines.

implementationPlan.description:
Adversarial self-review of this task's diff only. Load the adversarial-self-review skill first, then attack it:
- Hostile repo config in every scope (local, worktree, include.path, includeIf), replace refs, alternates, a sha256 repo, a shallow repo, split index, an index.lock left behind.
- Hostile env: GIT_*, HOME, a PATH holding a fake git, a Windows repo git.exe.
- Hostile candidates: a delete outside the base; writes beneath a base symlink or gitlink; D/F swaps; a case-variant path (note it as a residual for Windows/macOS checkouts, not a refusal in v1); a tampered manifest; 10,000 files; 256 MiB.
- Concurrency: two admissions, or an admission racing a wrapper landing on the same repo.

Check that:
- no ref, worktree or .git/index byte ever changes;
- the temp dir always goes;
- every refusal is one fixed code;
- export's behavior is unchanged;
- verified-local, executionReady and isolation claims are untouched;
- there is no .moe edit and no agent Git write. The admission's own object writes go to scratch repos in tests only.

Mutation spot-check in a scratch `git archive HEAD | tar -x` copy, scored by exit code with --test-name-pattern='^A[1-6] '. Mutants, and the row that should kill each:
- dropping --no-filters: A3;
- dropping core.hooksPath: A5 or A6;
- inheriting GIT_*: A5;
- a bare git allowed: A1;
- no delete-in-base check: A2;
- no ancestor or descendant conflict check: A2;
- no blob id cross-check: A3, with a wrapper that rewrites hash-object output;
- using the real index: A4;
- no temp cleanup: A6.

Fix anything found with a test, then re-run step 5's command fresh before complete_task. Report a follow-up, without fixing it here, that source-export.mjs still accepts a bare 'git'.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- LANDED, R09 DONE:
  - importCandidate resolves {instance, candidate: validateImport(entries), executionReady: false};
  - validateImport gives frozen {entries: [{kind:'file', path, executable, size, sha256, data} | {kind:'delete', path}] sorted by UTF-8, digest};
  - exportSourceSnapshot gives {version: 1, commit, tree, base, overlay, excluded};
  - source-export.mjs's private gitRunner sanitizes the env (no GIT_*, NOSYSTEM, GLOBAL=/dev/null or NUL, NO_LAZY_FETCH, TERMINAL_PROMPT=0), with GIT_PREFIX --no-optional-locks --no-replace-objects, protocol.allow=never, core.fsmonitor=false and safe.directory=<root>;
  - openCommit refuses partialclone, promisor, core.worktree and filter.* across every scope via no-scope `config --includes --get-regexp`.
- local-runner.test.mjs imports every module statically at the top, so add admission.mjs's import there. Test name prefixes in use are M, T and X; A is free.
- Git 2.43 on this box.
